{"id":"chatcmpl-9b6adf49-0d54-4243-be69-762d65ad6986","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246052,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question on a lateral chest X-ray where standard anatomical priors (right hemidiaphragm normally higher) create ambiguity between normal anatomy and pathology. The successful strategy combined multiple independent visual-question-answering models, then used a verification step to audit conflicting or garbled outputs before committing. The key insight is that lateral-view laterality is inherently ambiguous, so cross-model consensus plus explicit risk auditing is needed rather than trusting a single model.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on spatial laterality that is ambiguous in the given view, query multiple independent models and require consensus rather than trusting one output.\",\n    \"Before finalizing, run an explicit verification/audit step that names the specific ambiguity and conflicting evidence, so the answer is justified against known pitfalls.\",\n    \"Account for normal anatomical priors (e.g., one side normally higher) when interpreting 'elevated' findings, distinguishing pathology from baseline asymmetry.\",\n    \"Treat garbled or non-explicit model outputs as non-evidence; weight only clear, side-specific statements when aggregating votes.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Use 2-3 independent VLM/QA models for laterality or localization questions; require agreement and flag any model that fails to state the side explicitly.\",\n    \"Ambiguous-view interpretation\": \"When the imaging view makes the target feature ambiguous, lean on anatomical priors and cross-model consensus, and document the ambiguity in a verification step.\",\n    \"Multi-tool answer selection\": \"Aggregate tool outputs by clarity and specificity, not just count; a single clear statement can outweigh multiple vague ones, but confirm with a verifier.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm at least two models explicitly state the same side/laterality before answering.\",\n    \"Run a verification step that names the ambiguity and checks the proposed answer against anatomical priors and conflicting outputs.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":652,"total_tokens":1062,"completion_tokens":410,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":652},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":410}}}